in jQuery the enemy method performs a  custom animation of a set of CSS  properties this method changes an  element from one state to another with  CSS Styles the CSS property value is  changed gradually to create an animated  effect only numeric values can be  animated such as margin being 30 pixels  a string values cannot be animated such  as when you're setting the background  color to blue or red or something like  that so here's the basic syntax here so  first you're gonna have your element  selection and then it's going to be dot  animate and then you're gonna pass in  your properties your CSS properties that  you want to change and then there's  three optional things you can pass in  the duration easing and complete that's  just a callback function that it calls  when the animation is complete and  there's also another syntax this one  where you pass in the properties just  like before and then you pass in the  options this is just a JavaScript object  you pass in with various key value pairs  for different options this just allows  you to have a little more control than  the first method because there's a lot  of different options you can pass in  almost all the options have to do with  calling a callback function at various  points in the animation if you want more  information about the options you can  use for that you can check the link in  the description so let's look at this  example down here well first of all on  our page we just have the the run button  and the hello div block and then I just  have some basic CSS and here to style  things our JavaScript down here we're  going to select the the go button and  we're going to add a click function so  on click it's gonna run this function  here now inside the function we are  going to select the block which is that  the hello block and we're gonna run dot  animate the first thing we pass in is  the properties we have some key value  pairs that show the CSS properties we're  going to animate over the course of the  animation it's going to put all these  CSS properties to this value so it  starts at opacity 100% but we're going  to set it to 50%  so it's going to start at a hundred  percent and gradually go to 50 percent  here margin left now just so you know on  CSS will be margin - left but in jQuery  you take off the - and then you  capitalize the first letter of the  second word so you can see we use a  slightly different thing instead of  margin left 50 its margin left + equals  50 so it's just going to add 50 pixels  to whatever the margin already was for  the opacity it's always gonna go to 50%  and then height it's also going to go to  a specific thing 400 pixels and then the  next item you pass in is the duration so  I passed in 3000 that's 3,000  milliseconds or 3 seconds then we pass  an easing easing is either gonna be  swing or linear swing is the default so  if you don't pass in anything here it'll  just be swing or linear so linear just  moved at a constant rate swing kind of  eases in a little bit to the beginning  and the ending and then that complete  that's the callback function we're gonna  add at the end which we are going to  select this which is the div block that  we're animating and after that we're  going to add another HTML code when I  add this animation complete div so let's  see what this is gonna look like hit the  Run button and you can see the opacity  changes the margin left changes the  height changes and then the animation  complete runs at the bottom now let's  see what happens when I hit the Run  button again so as you can see the  opacity did not change the height did  not change what the margin left changed  where I press the Run button again  that's because we have this plus equals  50 so it just adds 50 to whatever the  value was but the other values are just  set so it's not going to change those  things and you can see it add the  animation complete div at the end  against there's two of them now I'm  going to take off this easing one so  it's gonna default to swing so let's see  what that looks like it's just a little  different so you can see just at the  beginning and ending of the animations  of little  now I'm just gonna actually change this  animation to show you how you can chain  animations so I'm just gonna get rid of  all this and then I'm gonna do dot  animate we're gonna set the width to 90%  I'm just gonna copy this and then paste  it a few times we're gonna change the  font size so now you can see I've  changed these animations so we're going  to change the width then the font size  then the border let left width let's see  what that looks like so you can see it  ran one animation after the other when  you just chained them by adding dot  animate and then putting the next  animation there and obviously within  each animation you can animate more than  one property but this is just an example  with one property okay that's the basics  of the dot animate method in jQuery  again check the link in the descriptions  for the other options you can use to  pass in which are mainly about different  callback functions you can use at  various points of animation my name is  Bo Carnes thanks for watching don't  forget to subscribe and remember use  your code for good
 

